// toolboxes/wavelet/src/filter/biorfilt.cpp
//
// Biorthogonal (bior*) and reverse-biorthogonal (rbio*) wavelet filter
// banks. Unlike the orthogonal families (haar/db/sym/coif, see
// wfilters.cpp), biorthogonal wavelets have DISTINCT analysis and
// synthesis filter pairs (Lo_D/Hi_D != Lo_R/Hi_R), so all four filters
// are tabulated independently (zero-padded to a common length, MATLAB
// convention). These are the Cohen-Daubechies-Feauveau spline
// biorthogonal coefficients (A. Cohen, I. Daubechies, J.-C. Feauveau,
// "Biorthogonal bases of compactly supported wavelets", Comm. Pure
// Appl. Math. 45 (1992) 485-560) -- mathematical constants reproduced
// identically across PyWavelets, the wavelet literature and MATLAB
// R2025b (against which numerical parity is checked in the harness).
//
// rbioNr.Nd is biorNr.Nd with the analysis/synthesis roles swapped.

